# Title: Maintenance Escalation
# Summary: A scalable operations benchmark where issue signals move through repeated review and repair stages.
# Benchmark Family: maintenance_escalation
# Repair_1: Operators coordinate a repair action at maintenance stage 1.
# Repair_2: Operators coordinate a repair action at maintenance stage 2.
# Review_1: Operators review the signal at maintenance stage 1.
# Review_2: Operators review the signal at maintenance stage 2.
# Signal_1: An issue signal is detected at maintenance stage 1.
# Signal_2: An issue signal is detected at maintenance stage 2.

prior_1: 0.122 <= P(Repair_1) <= 0.295
prior_2: 0.076 <= P(Repair_2) <= 0.302
prior_3: 0.0 <= P(Review_1) <= 0.203
prior_4: 0.168 <= P(Review_2) <= 0.372
prior_5: 0.249 <= P(Signal_1) <= 0.345
prior_6: 0.212 <= P(Signal_2) <= 0.39
component_1: 0.0 <= P(Repair_1 and Review_1) <= 0.203
component_2: 0.076 <= P(Repair_2 and Review_2) <= 0.302
link_1: 0.158 <= P(Repair_1 and Review_1 | Signal_1) <= 0.339
link_2: 0.17 <= P(Signal_2 | Repair_1 and Review_1) <= 0.236
link_3: 0.23 <= P(Repair_2 and Review_2 | Signal_2) <= 0.292
